			"notes": "# Modpack Installation Guide\n\n## Option 1: Install Using [Modrinth](https://modrinth.com/) (Recommended)\n\n1. Download the `.mrpack` file from the Modrinth page.  \n2. Open your Modrinth-compatible launcher (for example, the Modrinth App or Prism Launcher).  \n3. Click **\"Import Modpack\"** and select the downloaded `.mrpack` file.  \n4. The launcher will automatically install everything, including mods, settings, and saves.\n\n---\n\n## Option 2: Manual Installation\n\nIf you prefer to install the modpack manually, follow these steps:\n\n### 1. Install Fabric\n- Go to the [Fabric Installer](https://fabricmc.net/use/installer/).  \n- Download and run the Fabric Installer for **Minecraft 1.21.4**.  \n- Make sure the loader version is **0.14.18 or newer**.  \n- Click **Install** to create a Fabric profile in your Minecraft launcher.\n\n### 2. Add Mods and World\n- Unzip the provided .7z file.  \n- Move the extracted `mods` folder and the `testwelt` (world) folder into your new Fabric profile’s game directory.\n\nTypical locations:\n\n- Windows: %appdata%/.minecraft/\n- macOS: ~/Library/Application Support/minecraft/\n- Linux: ~/.minecraft/\n\n(For custom launchers, use the instance’s own game folder instead.)\n\n### 3. Launch Minecraft\n- Start Minecraft using your new Fabric profile.  \n- You should see your mods loaded and the `testwelt` world available to play.\n\n---\n\n**Tip:** If the game fails to launch, double-check that you’re using the correct Minecraft and Fabric versions."
		}
